Use of function pointers, static and external linkage, specialized libraries, and modular code organization to achieve reuse and abstraction in C:

// Function pointer declaration
return_type (*function_pointer_name)(parameter_types);

// Static and extern declarations for modularity
static return_type function_name(parameters);
extern return_type external_function_name(parameters);

// Usage of specialized libraries (e.g., math, data structures)
#include <math.h>
#include "datastructures.h"
